WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.920
Attention is a limited operational resource.

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.791
It allows people to hold goals in mind, reason through tradeoffs,

00:00:05.791 --> 00:00:08.280
notice important details, and resist distraction.

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.240
When attention is fragmented by notifications, context switching, open loops,

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.480
and competing demands,

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.205
the brain spends more effort reorienting and less effort doing the actual work.

00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:19.360
Deep work and shallow work both have a place.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.520
Deep work requires sustained focus, such as designing a system,

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.240
writing a careful analysis, debugging a difficult issue,

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:27.070
or making a high-consequence decision.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:31.040
Shallow work includes status updates, quick messages, routine coordination,

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.095
and simple administrative tasks.

00:00:33.095 --> 00:00:36.800
Performance improves when these modes are managed intentionally instead of mixed together

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:37.530
all day.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:41.910
Cognitive load is the mental effort required to hold, process, and use information.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:45.965
Working memory is limited, so systems should not force people to remember every next step,

00:00:45.965 --> 00:00:47.911
dependency, decision, and deadline.

00:00:47.911 --> 00:00:51.120
Checklists, notes, visible task boards, calendars, templates,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.305
and clear handoffs reduce unnecessary load.

00:00:53.305 --> 00:00:56.840
The goal is to let the brain work on the problem, not on remembering the workspace.

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.475
Practical focus management includes batching similar tasks, protecting focus blocks,

00:01:01.475 --> 00:01:04.275
reducing unnecessary notifications, closing open loops,

00:01:04.275 --> 00:01:06.300
and separating planning from execution.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.440
If every task arrives as an interruption, performance becomes reactive.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.120
A better design gives people clear priorities, fewer unnecessary resets,

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.195
and trusted places to capture work that should not be held in memory.

00:01:16.195 --> 00:01:19.400
A useful test is to ask what the work is making the person remember.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.925
If success depends on remembering every dependency, promise, exception,

00:01:22.925 --> 00:01:25.285
and deadline unaided, the system is fragile.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:28.140
Externalizing that information through notes, queues, calendars,

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.975
and shared artifacts is not weakness.

00:01:29.975 --> 00:01:33.730
It is a professional way to protect attention for the work that requires judgment.
